    "description": "Search recent X (Twitter) posts, newest first, through RSSHub's configured Twitter backend. \`query\` is sent verbatim to X search; it is not URL-encoded or rewritten. Returns up to \`limit\` posts from one upstream page. To get older posts, pass the result's \`nextCursor\` as \`cursor\` with the same \`query\`. A missing \`nextCursor\` means there are no more results. Every call is a fresh read. Requires RSSHub Twitter credentials: TWITTER_AUTH_TOKEN, TWITTER_THIRD_PARTY_API, or TWITTER_CONSUMER_KEY + TWITTER_CONSUMER_SECRET (developer API, last 7 days only).",
